flowchart TB
  accTitle: ENS402 namespace and contract tree
  accDescr: ens402.eth points to Platform Registry A. Its company name points to Company Registry B. Three service names each point to a separate resolver C1, C2 or C3. Each resolver stores an API URL, payment settings and status. Wallet permissions are listed separately below the diagram.
  parent["ens402.eth"]
  platform["A · Platform Registry"]
  company["company.ens402.eth"]
  registry["B · Company Registry"]
  s1["service1"]
  s2["service2"]
  s3["service3"]
  r1["C1<br/>Resolver 1"]
  r2["C2<br/>Resolver 2"]
  r3["C3<br/>Resolver 3"]
  parent -->|subregistry| platform
  platform -.->|name entry| company
  company -->|subregistry| registry
  registry -.->|name entry| s1 & s2 & s3
  s1 -->|resolver| r1
  s2 -->|resolver| r2
  s3 -->|resolver| r3
  classDef registry fill:#f4f5f7,stroke:#abb4c2,stroke-width:1.5px
  classDef resolver fill:#f0f5ff,stroke:#7298df,stroke-width:1.5px
  class platform,registry registry
  class r1,r2,r3 resolver
